type": "text", "content": "Can you really understand the idea of the future of old age? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: \nOrganize the mystery sentence. Move each word to place it in the correct order."}]}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le12ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "What is the future of old age? To answer that question and to shine a light on the issue, we need to reconsider our conventional notion of life, aging, and death.  During the past one hundred years, life expectancy has doubled. People are living longer because of better nutrition (more vegetables, less chocolate - or at least the right kind of chocolate, a glass of red wine a day), healthier lifestyles, and incredible advances in healthcare and medical science."}, {"time": "31000", "image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Philosophers, doctors and scientists have been striving for that fountain of youth since the beginning of recorded history. We all want to live forever, right?We all want to reach our diamond wedding anniversary, don't we?<br/>\nFor some in the medical community, their lofty, but interesting goal is to redefine the very nature of human life.  Their research focuses on extending the deadline of the human lifespan, extending our lives for hundreds or even thousands of years. However, there are many people who question whether immortality should even be considered - that it should remain up to the divine powers."}, {"time": "76500", "image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "The newest and most ambitious ideas are about integrating humans and technology to create beings that can live for thousands of years. We've all seen Terminator, haven't we? This is the most dangerous of all pursuits, isn't it?"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Future of Old Age"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le12ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Silent Syllables in Which Unstressed Vowels are not Pronounced "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>Syllables are the sound groupings in words. </p><p>For example:<br/>Ca - na - da <br/>Com - pu - ter</p><p>Usually, you pronounce each syllable in a word.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some words in English have syllables which are not pronounced."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some examples are:<br/> vegetable  ----->  veg**table<br/> chocolate -----> choc**late<br/> diamond ------> di**mond<br/> interesting ----> int**res**ting<br/>dangerous -----> dang**rous"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice saying the words above. Clap each time you say a syllable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "People are living longer because of better nutrition (more vegetables, less chocolate - or at least the right kind of chocolate, a glass of red wine a day)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "For some in the medical community, their lofty, but interesting goal is to redefine the very nature of human life. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is the most dangerous of all pursuits, isn't it? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Words That End in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, many words share similar endings. One of common ending is <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Generally, when a word ends with the vowel <span class=\"strong\">e</span>, the vowel that comes before it is pronounced with its long sound. You can see this rule when you read and say words that end in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/>f - <span class=\"strong\">i</span> - n - <span class=\"strong\">e</span>  ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">i</span> ( as in the word <span class=\"italic\">eye</span>)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can see this rule at work in other words and for other sounds. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/>g - <span class=\"strong\">a</span> - m- <span class=\"strong\">e</span> ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">a</span> (as in the word <span class=\"italic\">day</span>)<br/>b - <span class=\"strong\">o</span> - n - <span class=\"strong\">e</span> ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">o</span> (as in the word <span class=\"italic\">go</span>)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some examples of words that end in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>.<br/><span class=\"italic\">fine <br/>dine <br/>wine <br/>line <br/>redefine <br/>shine <br/>deadline <br/>divine</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading these sentences aloud. Focus on the pronunciation of the <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span> sound.<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>It should remain up to the div<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> powers. </li><li>Their lofty, but interesting goal is to redef<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> the very nature of human life.  </li><li>To answer that question and to sh<span class=\"italic\">ine</span> a light on the issue, we need to reconsider our conventional notion of life.</li><li>A glass of red w<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> a day</li></ul></span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conventional "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "traditional; related to tradition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to reconsider our conventional notion of life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about staying healthy."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "notion "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "idea; point of view"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need a different notion of life to understand the future of old age."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "life expectancy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the projected duration of a person's life "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Life expectancy has doubled during the past 100 years."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "philosopher "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who studies topics related to ethics or metaphysics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Philosophers have looked for a fountain of youth."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "diamond wedding anniversary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a celebration of the 60th year of marriage "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We all want to reach our diamond wedding anniversary."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lofty "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very high; eminent"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Their lofty but interesting goal is to redefine the nature of human life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "immortality "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the condition of perpetual life"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Should immortality be considered?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pursuit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of looking for something, especially a goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Integrating humans and technology to create immortals is a dangerous pursuit."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le12ob04aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find the movie <span class=\"italic\">The Terminator</span> online or at your video store."}, {"type": "text", "content": "As you watch the movie, think about the idea of integrating technology and humans."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss the movie and the implications it has for the future of old age."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">The Terminator</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I consider the idea of integrating technology and humans."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the movie with a partner."}]}]}